Find the number of ordered pairs $(x,y)$ of real numbers satisfying
\begin{align*}
y &= 4 g(f(\sin (2 \pi x))) \text{ and} \\
x &= 4 g(f(\cos (3 \pi y))).
\end{align*}

Consider the function \[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
x^2 & \text{if } x \leq 0, \\
2x & \text{if } x > 0.
\end{array}
\right.\] and \[g(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
x^3 & \text{if } x \leq 0, \\
x & \text{if } x > 0.
\end{array}
\right.\] Find the number of intersections of the graphs of \[y = 2f(g(\sin (2 \pi x)))\] and \[x = 2g(f(\cos (3 \pi y))).\]
